Subject: [PATCH] eglplatform_fbdev: open and prime the framebuffer in init_module

The vendor (Mali/Amlogic) gralloc caches the fb geometry on the first
framebuffer open/allocation. With the reopen-at-CreateWindow change this
first open happened after the application had already switched to a small
resolution (e.g. 720p), so switching up later gave wrong buffer offsets.
Open and allocate/free one HW_FB buffer in init_module as well.
---
--- a/egl/platforms/fbdev/eglplatform_fbdev.cpp
+++ b/egl/platforms/fbdev/eglplatform_fbdev.cpp
@@ -35,6 +35,24 @@
 		assert(0);
 	}
 	TRACE("** gralloc_open %p status=%s", gralloc, strerror(-err));
+
+	/*
+	 * The vendor gralloc caches the framebuffer geometry (and buffer layout)
+	 * when the framebuffer is opened/allocated for the first time in the
+	 * process. Do it here, while fb0 still has the size set by the
+	 * application before EGL initialization (largest GUI size), otherwise a
+	 * later switch to a larger resolution leaves wrong buffer offsets.
+	 * The framebuffer is re-opened in fbdevws_CreateWindow() as before.
+	 */
+	err = framebuffer_open((hw_module_t *) gralloc, &framebuffer);
+	if (err == 0 && framebuffer) {
+		buffer_handle_t handle = NULL;
+		int stride = 0;
+		if (alloc->alloc(alloc, framebuffer->width, framebuffer->height,
+				framebuffer->format, GRALLOC_USAGE_HW_FB, &handle, &stride) == 0)
+			alloc->free(alloc, handle);
+		TRACE("** framebuffer primed: %dx%d", framebuffer->width, framebuffer->height);
+	}
 	eglplatformcommon_init(egl_iface, gralloc, alloc);
 }
 
